    "composition_parti": {
      "group": "massing-and-roof",
      "binding": "specified",
      "status": "drafted",
      "confidence": "high",
      "judgment": true,
      "rule": "There is no composed principal elevation: the exterior street wall is high, blind and undesigned (see `street_relationship`). Composition happens on the plan, in the sequence of courts -- and there, at the scale of a single court, the arrangement is bilaterally symmetrical about its long axis, with a hall at each end (e.g. the Court of the Myrtles). This is a plan symmetry, not a composed facade the building does not have.",
      "note": "OVERRIDES a cascade fill from antique-classical ('The principal elevation is strictly bilaterally symmetrical about a central axis'), which is correct only if misapplied from plan to elevation -- this node's own text is explicit that 'there is no facade in the ordinary sense: the exterior wall is high, blind, and... undesigned' (description) and that composition governs 'the court, the water in it, and the way light moves across it' rather than an elevation. The antique-classical figure reaches this node only through a real but narrow lineage edge to roman-classical (descends_from, weight 0.35, reused Roman columns/capitals and the horseshoe arch's Visigothic root) that was never meant to license a composed classical FACADE this node explicitly does not have. Fixed here per WP-4.2 instructions rather than on any ancestor kit."
    },
